'''Super Wrath''' is a [[mini-boss]] and one of the [[Seven Deadly Sins#Super Sins|Seven Super Deadly Sins]]. He is randomly encountered as an alternate version of {{e|Wrath}}.

== Behavior ==
* Super Wrath wanders around the room randomly, spawning {{e|Mega Troll Bomb}}s on his position.
** Super Wrath takes only 20 damage (not the usual {{dlc|nr}} 60 / {{dlc|r}} 100) from his own bombs.
* Super Wrath deals a full heart of damage (both bombs and contact).

== Notes ==
* In a mini-boss room, Super Wrath can spawn near 2 {{e|Mega Troll Bomb}}s.
* Isaac's bombs and {{i|Epic Fetus}} missiles deal 200 damage regardless of modifiers or damage stat.
* {{dlc|nr}} Super Wrath can drop {{i|Mr. Mega}} even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed it. 
* {{t|Safety Scissors}} replaces the Mega Troll Bombs with {{e|Double Bomb}} drops.
* {{i|Pyromaniac}} or {{i|Host Hat}} renders Super Wrath unable to damage Isaac with bombs. Explosions can still knock Isaac into hazards.

== Trivia ==
* Super Wrath's blasted and soot-covered appearance suggests a backfired or failed attempt to handle a bomb.
* {{e|Wrath}} and Super Wrath bear a strong resemblance to the title character of the [[wikipedia:Bomberman|''Bomberman'']] series, both in their appearance and their attack patterns.
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived.

